<title>POLAND: More Kredyt Bank shares for bourse trade.</title>
<headline>More Kredyt Bank shares for bourse trade.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish Kredyt Bank SA will add 12 million shares, issued last year, to those already traded on the Warsaw bourse on March 21, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>The bank said that, after the assimilation, it would have altogether 25,149,188 shares traded on the exchange.</p>
<p>It has a total share capital of 25,631,304 shares. Under Warsaw bourse rules, not all issued shares are immediately admitted for trading.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
